  "worked_solution": "The cardinality of a finite set $B$ is the number of elements in $B.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $B:$\n\n$$\n0,\\,1,\\,2\n$$\n\nNote that only *unique* elements are counted. In other words, duplicate elements are *not* counted separately.\n\nSince $B$ has $3$ elements, its cardinality is $|B|=3.$",
